text: ['All creatures get -3/-3 until end of turn.\\nYou may cast a spell with mana value 3 or less from your hand without paying its mana cost.', 'As Metallic Mimic enters the battlefield, choose a creature type.\\nMetallic Mimic is the chosen type in addition to its other types.\\nEach other creature you control of the chosen type enters the battlefield with an additional +1/+1 counter on it.', 'At end of combat, if Daredevil Dragster attacked or blocked this combat, put a velocity counter on it. Then if it has two or more velocity counters on it, sacrifice it and draw two cards.\\nCrew 2 (Tap any number of creatures you control with total power 2 or more: This Vehicle becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.)', 'At the beginning of combat on your turn, target artifact creature you control gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, scry 1.\\nWhenever you cast a creature spell, you may pay {G}. If you do, draw a card.', "Audacious Infiltrator can't be blocked by artifact creatures.", "Chandra's Revolution deals 4 damage to target creature. Tap target land. That land doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", "Choose one —\\n• Destroy target artifact.\\n• Creatures without flying can't block this turn.", 'Choose one —\\n• Target creature gets +4/+0 and gains trample until end of turn.\\n• Two target creatures each get +2/+0 and gain trample until end of turn.', "Choose one —\\n• Target creature you control gets +1/+2 until end of turn.\\n• Return target creature you control to its owner's hand.", 'Counter target noncreature spell.', "Counter target spell, activated ability, or triggered ability. (Mana abilities can't be targeted.)", 'Create three 1/1 colorless Servo artifact creature tokens.\\nYou may cast a spell with mana value 3 or less from your hand without paying its mana cost.', 'Crew 3 (Tap any number of creatures you control with total power 3 or more: This Vehicle becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.)', 'Crew 6 (Tap any number of creatures you control with total power 6 or more: This Vehicle becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.)', 'Deathtouch (Any amount of damage this deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)\\nWhen Aether Poisoner enters the battlefield, you get {E}{E} (two energy counters).\\nWhenever Aether Poisoner attacks, you may pay {E}{E}. If you do, create a 1/1 colorless Servo artifact creature token.', 'Deathtouch, lifelink', 'Deathtouch\\nRevolt — Narnam Renegade enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it if a permanent you controlled left the battlefield this turn.', 'Deft Dismissal deals 3 damage divided as you choose among one, two, or three target attacking or blocking creatures.', 'Destroy X target artifacts and/or creatures. For each permanent destroyed this way, its controller reveals cards from the top of their library until an artifact or creature card is revealed and exiles that card. Those players put the exiled cards onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'Destroy X target artifacts. Create X 2/2 red Gremlin creature tokens.', 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment.\\nRevolt — If a permanent you controlled left the battlefield this turn, you gain 3 life.', 'Destroy target creature if it has mana value 2 or less.\\nRevolt — Destroy that creature if it has mana value 4 or less instead if a permanent you controlled left the battlefield this turn.', 'Destroy target creature or Vehicle.', 'Destroy target creature. You may search your library and/or graveyard for a card named Tezzeret, Master of Metal, reveal it, and put it into your hand. If you search your library this way, shuffle.', 'Double strike (This creature deals both first-strike and regular combat damage.)\\nWhen Scrapper Champion enters the battlefield, you get {E}{E} (two energy counters).\\nWhenever Scrapper Champion attacks, you may pay {E}{E}. If you do, put a +1/+1 counter on it.', 'Double strike, haste\\nWhenever Lightning Runner attacks, you get {E}{E} (two energy counters), then you may pay {E}{E}{E}{E}{E}{E}{E}{E}. If you pay, untap all creatures you control, and after this phase, there is an additional combat phase.', 'Double strike\\nRevolt — At the beginning of your end step, if a permanent you controlled left the battlefield this turn, put a +1/+1 counter on Solemn Recruit.', 'Draw cards equal to the greatest power among creatures you control.\\nYou may cast a spell with mana value 5 or less from your hand without paying its mana cost.', 'Each opponent sacrifices a creature or planeswalker, then discards a card. You return a creature or planeswalker card from your graveyard to your hand, then draw a card.\\nWhen you cast a Bolas planeswalker spell, exile Dark Intimations from your graveyard. That planeswalker enters the battlefield with an additional loyalty counter on it.', 'Each opponent sacrifices an artifact creature and a nonartifact creature.', "Enchant artifact or creature\\nEnchanted permanent doesn't untap during its controller's untap step.", "Enchant artifact you control\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, create a token that's a copy of enchanted artifact. Then if you control eight or more artifacts with the same name as one another, you win the game.", "Enchant artifact\\nAt the beginning of your end step, Gremlin Infestation deals 2 damage to enchanted artifact's controller.\\nWhen enchanted artifact is put into a graveyard, create a 2/2 red Gremlin creature token.", "Enchant artifact\\nEnchanted artifact is a creature with base power and toughness 5/5 in addition to its other types.\\nWhen enchanted artifact is put into a graveyard, return that card to its owner's hand.", "Enchant creature or Vehicle\\nAs long as enchanted permanent is a Vehicle, it's a creature in addition to its other types.\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 and has flying.", "Enchant creature or Vehicle\\nAs long as enchanted permanent is a Vehicle, it's a creature in addition to its other types.\\nEnchanted creature gets +3/+0 and has first strike.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block.\\nWhen a Vehicle you control attacks, exile enchanted creature.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+3.\\n{W}: Return Conviction to its owner's hand.", 'Enchant land\\nEnchanted land has "{T}: Add one mana of any color."\\nSacrifice Unbridled Growth: Draw a card.', 'Exile target nonland card from your graveyard. Search your library for any number of cards with the same name as that card, reveal them, put them into your hand, then shuffle.', "Exile up to two target creatures you control, then return those cards to the battlefield under their owner's control.\\nDraw a card.", 'First strike, menace\\nWhenever Kari Zev, Skyship Raider attacks, create Ragavan, a legendary 2/1 red Monkey creature token. Ragavan enters the battlefield tapped and attacking. Exile that token at end of combat.', 'First strike\\nWhen Aether Chaser enters the battlefield, you get {E}{E} (two energy counters).\\nWhenever Aether Chaser attacks, you may pay {E}{E}. If you do, create a 1/1 colorless Servo artifact creature token.', 'First strike\\nWhenever Reckless Racer becomes tapped, you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.', 'Flash (You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.)\\nWhenever Shielded Aether Thief blocks, you get {E} (an energy counter).\\n{T}, Pay {E}{E}{E}: Draw a card.', 'Flying', "Flying, vigilance\\nCrew 3 (Tap any number of creatures you control with total power 3 or more: This Vehicle becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.)\\nYou may remove a loyalty counter from a planeswalker you control rather than pay Heart of Kiran's crew cost.", "Flying\\nHinterland Drake can't block artifact creatures.", 'Flying\\nIf you would lose the game, instead exile Exquisite Archangel and your life total becomes equal to your starting life total.', 'Flying\\nRevolt — Night Market Aeronaut enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it if a permanent you controlled left the battlefield this turn.', 'Flying\\nRevolt — When Airdrop Aeronauts enters the battlefield, if a permanent you controlled left the battlefield this turn, you gain 5 life.', "Flying\\nSacrifice Hope of Ghirapur: Until your next turn, target player who was dealt combat damage by Hope of Ghirapur this turn can't cast noncreature spells.", 'Flying\\nVehicles you control have flying.', 'Flying\\nWhen Aether Swooper enters the battlefield, you get {E}{E} (two energy counters).\\nWhenever Aether Swooper attacks, you may pay {E}{E}. If you do, create a 1/1 colorless Servo artifact creature token.', 'Flying\\nWhen Aethersphere Harvester enters the battlefield, you get {E}{E} (two energy counters).\\nPay {E}: Aethersphere Harvester gains lifelink until end of turn.\\nCrew 1 (Tap any number of creatures you control with total power 1 or more: This Vehicle becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.)', "Flying\\nWhen Aethertide Whale enters the battlefield, you get {E}{E}{E}{E}{E}{E} (six energy counters).\\nPay {E}{E}{E}{E}: Return Aethertide Whale to its owner's hand.", 'Flying\\nWhen Dawnfeather Eagle enters the battlefield, creatures you control get +1/+1 and gain vigilance until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nWhen Foundry Hornet enters the battlefield, if you control a creature with a +1/+1 counter on it, creatures your opponents control get -1/-1 until end of turn.', "Flying\\nWhen Spire Patrol enters the battlefield, tap target creature an opponent controls. That creature doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", 'Flying\\nWhenever Skyship Plunderer deals combat damage to a player, for each kind of counter on target permanent or player, give that permanent or player another counter of that kind.', 'Frontline Rebel attacks each combat if able.', 'Gain control of target creature or Vehicle until end of turn. Untap it. It gains haste until end of turn.\\nYou may cast a spell with mana value 2 or less from your hand without paying its mana cost.', 'Gain control of target creature with power 4 or less until end of turn. Untap that creature. It gains haste until end of turn.', 'Haste\\nWhenever a creature an opponent controls dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Yahenni, Undying Partisan.\\nSacrifice another creature: Yahenni gains indestructible until end of turn.', 'Hungry Flames deals 3 damage to target creature and 2 damage to target player or planeswalker.', 'If one or more counters would be put on an artifact or creature you control, that many plus one of each of those kinds of counters are put on that permanent instead.\\nIf you would get one or more counters, you get that many plus one of each of those kinds of counters instead.', "Improvise (Your artifacts can help cast this spell. Each artifact you tap after you're done activating mana abilities pays for {1}.)", "Improvise (Your artifacts can help cast this spell. Each artifact you tap after you're done activating mana abilities pays for {1}.)\\nBarricade Breaker attacks each combat if able.", "Improvise (Your artifacts can help cast this spell. Each artifact you tap after you're done activating mana abilities pays for {1}.)\\nCounter target spell unless its controller pays {3}.", "Improvise (Your artifacts can help cast this spell. Each artifact you tap after you're done activating mana abilities pays for {1}.)\\nDraw three cards.", "Improvise (Your artifacts can help cast this spell. Each artifact you tap after you're done activating mana abilities pays for {1}.)\\nFen Hauler can't be blocked by artifact creatures.", "Improvise (Your artifacts can help cast this spell. Each artifact you tap after you're done activating mana abilities pays for {1}.)\\nFlying", "Improvise (Your artifacts can help cast this spell. Each artifact you tap after you're done activating mana abilities pays for {1}.)\\nFlying\\nAt the beginning of your end step, each opponent discards a card.\\n{1}{B}, Sacrifice an artifact: Target creature gets -2/-2 until end of turn.", "Improvise (Your artifacts can help cast this spell. Each artifact you tap after you're done activating mana abilities pays for {1}.)\\nFlying\\n{1}{R}: Freejam Regent gets +2/+0 until end of turn.", "Improvise (Your artifacts can help cast this spell. Each artifact you tap after you're done activating mana abilities pays for {1}.)\\nHexproof (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)", "Improvise (Your artifacts can help cast this spell. Each artifact you tap after you're done activating mana abilities pays for {1}.)\\nMenace", "Improvise (Your artifacts can help cast this spell. Each artifact you tap after you're done activating mana abilities pays for {1}.)\\nSearch your library for an artifact card with mana value X or less, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.", "Improvise (Your artifacts can help cast this spell. Each artifact you tap after you're done activating mana abilities pays for {1}.)\\nTarget creature gets -X/-X until end of turn. You gain X life.", "Improvise (Your artifacts can help cast this spell. Each artifact you tap after you're done activating mana abilities pays for {1}.)\\nTrample, haste", "Improvise (Your artifacts can help cast this spell. Each artifact you tap after you're done activating mana abilities pays for {1}.)\\nWhen Maverick Thopterist enters the battlefield, create two 1/1 colorless Thopter artifact creature tokens with flying.", "Improvise (Your artifacts can help cast this spell. Each artifact you tap after you're done activating mana abilities pays for {1}.)\\nWhenever a nontoken artifact you control is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, create a 1/1 colorless Servo artifact creature token.", 'Instant and sorcery spells you cast cost {1} less to cast.\\nWhenever a spell or ability you control counters a spell, you may draw a card. If you do, discard a card.', 'Menace', 'Menace\\nWhenever Glint-Sleeve Siphoner enters the battlefield or attacks, you get {E} (an energy counter).\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may pay {E}{E}. If you do, you draw a card and you lose 1 life.', 'Monstrous Onslaught deals X damage divided as you choose among any number of target creatures, where X is the greatest power among creatures you control as you cast this spell.', 'Night Market Guard can block an additional creature each combat.', "Nonartifact spells you cast have improvise. (Your artifacts can help cast those spells. Each artifact you tap after you're done activating mana abilities pays for {1}.)", 'Other Aetherborn you control get +1/+1.\\nWhenever Midnight Entourage or another Aetherborn you control dies, you draw a card and you lose 1 life.', "Outland Boar can't be blocked by creatures with power 2 or less.", 'Permanents you control gain hexproof and indestructible until end of turn.', "Put X +1/+1 counters on target artifact you control. If it isn't a creature or Vehicle, it becomes a 0/0 Construct artifact creature.", 'Put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control.', 'Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature, then put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it.', "Put target artifact on the bottom of its owner's library.", 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nRevolt — When Silkweaver Elite enters the battlefield, if a permanent you controlled left the battlefield this turn, draw a card.', 'Renegade Map enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Renegade Map: Search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand. If you control an artifact, draw a card.', "Return target nonland permanent to its owner's hand.\\nDraw a card.", "Return up to three target artifacts and/or creatures to their owners' hands.\\nYou may cast a spell with mana value 4 or less from your hand without paying its mana cost.", 'Revolt — At the beginning of your end step, if a permanent you controlled left the battlefield this turn, create a 1/1 colorless Servo artifact creature token.\\n{1}, Sacrifice a creature: Scry 1.', 'Revolt — At the beginning of your end step, if a permanent you controlled left the battlefield this turn, put a unity counter on Call for Unity.\\nCreatures you control get +1/+1 for each unity counter on Call for Unity.', "Revolt — At the beginning of your end step, if a permanent you controlled left the battlefield this turn, reveal the top card of your library. If it's a permanent card, you may put it onto the battlefield. Otherwise, you may put it on the bottom of your library.", 'Revolt — Greenwheel Liberator enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it if a permanent you controlled left the battlefield this turn.', 'Revolt — When Countless Gears Renegade enters the battlefield, if a permanent you controlled left the battlefield this turn, create a 1/1 colorless Servo artifact creature token.', 'Revolt — When Deadeye Harpooner enters the battlefield, if a permanent you controlled left the battlefield this turn, destroy target tapped creature an opponent controls.', 'Revolt — When Hidden Herbalists enters the battlefield, if a permanent you controlled left the battlefield this turn, add {G}{G}.', 'Revolt — When Renegade Rallier enters the battlefield, if a permanent you controlled left the battlefield this turn, return target permanent card with mana value 2 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'Revolt — When Vengeful Rebel enters the battlefield, if a permanent you controlled left the battlefield this turn, target creature an opponent controls gets -3/-3 until end of turn.', 'Sacrifice an artifact or creature: Put a +1/+1 counter on Defiant Salvager. Activate only as a sorcery.', 'Sacrifice an artifact: Ravenous Intruder gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Scrounging Bandar enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may move any number of +1/+1 counters from Scrounging Bandar onto another target creature.', 'Shock deals 2 damage to any target.', 'Submerged Boneyard enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}.', "Tap target creature. It doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", 'Target creature gets +1/+0 and gains first strike until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn. You get {E}{E} (two energy counters).', 'Target creature gets -2/-2 until end of turn. Scry 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put that card on the bottom of your library.)', "Target creature you control fights target creature you don't control. (Each deals damage equal to its power to the other.)", 'Target permanent gains indestructible until end of turn. Create a 1/1 colorless Servo artifact creature token. (Effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy a permanent with indestructible, and if it\'s a creature, it can\'t be destroyed by damage.)', "Trample\\nAt the beginning of combat on your turn, if you control an Ajani planeswalker, put a +1/+1 counter on Ajani's Comrade.", 'Trample\\nRevolt — Lifecraft Cavalry enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it if a permanent you controlled left the battlefield this turn.', 'Trample\\nWhen Aetherstream Leopard enters the battlefield, you get {E} (an energy counter).\\nWhenever Aetherstream Leopard attacks, you may pay {E}. If you do, it gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'Trample\\nWhen Maulfist Revolutionary enters the battlefield or dies, for each kind of counter on target permanent or player, give that permanent or player another counter of that kind.', 'Trample\\nWhenever Aetherwind Basker enters the battlefield or attacks, you get {E} (an energy counter) for each creature you control.\\nPay {E}: Aetherwind Basker gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Trample\\nWhenever Untethered Express attacks, put a +1/+1 counter on it.\\nCrew 1 (Tap any number of creatures you control with total power 1 or more: This Vehicle becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.)', 'Tranquil Expanse enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}.', 'Vigilance\\nWhen Aether Inspector enters the battlefield, you get {E}{E} (two energy counters).\\nWhenever Aether Inspector attacks, you may pay {E}{E}. If you do, create a 1/1 colorless Servo artifact creature token.', 'Walking Ballista enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{4}: Put a +1/+1 counter on Walking Ballista.\\nRemove a +1/+1 counter from Walking Ballista: It deals 1 damage to any target.', 'When Aether Herder enters the battlefield, you get {E}{E} (two energy counters).\\nWhenever Aether Herder attacks, you may pay {E}{E}. If you do, create a 1/1 colorless Servo artifact creature token.', "When Ajani's Aid enters the battlefield, you may search your library and/or graveyard for a card named Ajani, Valiant Protector, reveal it, and put it into your hand. If you search your library this way, shuffle.\\nSacrifice Ajani's Aid: Prevent all combat damage a creature of your choice would deal this turn.", 'When Consulate Crackdown enters the battlefield, exile all artifacts your opponents control until Consulate Crackdown leaves the battlefield.', "When Dispersal Technician enters the battlefield, you may return target artifact to its owner's hand.", "When Felidar Guardian enters the battlefield, you may exile another target permanent you control, then return that card to the battlefield under its owner's control.", 'When Filigree Crawler dies, create a 1/1 colorless Thopter artifact creature token with flying.', 'When Fourth Bridge Prowler enters the battlefield, you may have target creature get -1/-1 until end of turn.', "When Greenbelt Rampager enters the battlefield, pay {E}{E} (two energy counters). If you can't, return Greenbelt Rampager to its owner's hand and you get {E}.", 'When Ironclad Revolutionary enters the battlefield, you may sacrifice an artifact. If you do, put two +1/+1 counters on Ironclad Revolutionary and each opponent loses 2 life.', 'When Oath of Ajani enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control.\\nPlaneswalker spells you cast cost {1} less to cast.', 'When Peema Aether-Seer enters the battlefield, you get an amount of {E} (energy counters) equal to the greatest power among creatures you control.\\nPay {E}{E}{E}: Target creature blocks this turn if able.', 'When Pendulum of Patterns enters the battlefield, you gain 3 life.\\n{5}, {T}, Sacrifice Pendulum of Patterns: Draw a card.', 'When Quicksmith Rebel enters the battlefield, target artifact you control gains "{T}: This artifact deals 2 damage to any target" for as long as you control Quicksmith Rebel.', 'When Quicksmith Spy enters the battlefield, target artifact you control gains "{T}: Draw a card" for as long as you control Quicksmith Spy.', 'When Reservoir Walker enters the battlefield, you gain 3 life and get {E}{E}{E} (three energy counters).', 'When Ridgescale Tusker enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on each other creature you control.', 'When Rishkar, Peema Renegade enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on each of up to two target creatures.\\nEach creature you control with a counter on it has "{T}: Add {G}."', 'When Rogue Refiner enters the battlefield, draw a card and you get {E}{E} (two energy counters).', 'When Servo Schematic enters the battlefield or is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, create a 1/1 colorless Servo artifact creature token.', 'When Shipwreck Moray enters the battlefield, you get {E}{E}{E}{E} (four energy counters).\\nPay {E}: Shipwreck Moray gets +2/-2 until end of turn.', 'When Thopter Arrest enters the battlefield, exile target artifact or creature an opponent controls until Thopter Arrest leaves the battlefield.', 'When Treasure Keeper dies, reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal a nonland card with mana value 3 or less. You may cast that card without paying its mana cost. Put all revealed cards not cast this way on the bottom of your library in a random order.', 'When Trophy Mage enters the battlefield, you may search your library for an artifact card with mana value 3, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', "Whenever Aethergeode Miner attacks, you get {E}{E} (two energy counters).\\nPay {E}{E}: Exile Aethergeode Miner, then return it to the battlefield under its owner's control.", "Whenever Gonti's Aether Heart or another artifact enters the battlefield under your control, you get {E}{E} (two energy counters).\\nPay {E}{E}{E}{E}{E}{E}{E}{E}, Exile Gonti's Aether Heart: Take an extra turn after this one.", 'Whenever Mobile Garrison attacks, untap another target artifact or creature you control.\\nCrew 2 (Tap any number of creatures you control with total power 2 or more: This Vehicle becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.)', "Whenever Renegade Wheelsmith becomes tapped, target creature can't block this turn.", "Whenever Salvage Scuttler attacks, return an artifact you control to its owner's hand.", 'Whenever Scrap Trawler or another artifact you control is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, return to your hand target artifact card in your graveyard with lesser mana value.', "Whenever a nontoken artifact is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, return that card to your hand unless target opponent has Pia's Revolution deal 3 damage to them.", "Whenever you activate an ability of an artifact or creature that isn't a mana ability, Crackdown Construct gets +1/+1 until end of turn.", 'Whenever you cast a spell, untap all nonland permanents you control.', 'Whenever you cast an Aura, Equipment, or Vehicle spell, draw a card.', 'Whenever you cast an artifact spell, create a 1/1 colorless Thopter artifact creature token with flying.', "Whenever you lose life for the first time each turn, you get {E}. (You get an energy counter. Damage causes loss of life.)\\nPay {E}{E}, Sacrifice Gonti's Machinations: Each opponent loses 3 life. You gain life equal to the life lost this way.", '[+1]: Create a colorless artifact token named Etherium Cell with "{T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Add one mana of any color."\\n[−2]: Target creature gets +X/-X until end of turn, where X is the number of artifacts you control.\\n[−7]: You get an emblem with "At the beginning of combat on your turn, target artifact you control becomes an artifact creature with base power and toughness 5/5."', '[+1]: Reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal an artifact card. Put that card into your hand and the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.\\n[−3]: Target opponent loses life equal to the number of artifacts you control.\\n[−8]: Gain control of all artifacts and creatures target opponent controls.', '[+2]: Put two +1/+1 counters on up to one target creature.\\n[+1]: Reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal a creature card. Put that card into your hand and the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.\\n[−11]: Put X +1/+1 counters on target creature, where X is your life total. That creature gains trample until end of turn.', '[+2]: Reveal the top three cards of your library. Put all nonland permanent cards revealed this way into your hand and the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.\\n[−2]: Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.\\n[−9]: Put five +1/+1 counters on each creature you control and five loyalty counters on each other planeswalker you control.', '{1}{B}: Augmenting Automaton gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{1}{W}: Another target Vehicle you control becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.\\nCrew 4 (Tap any number of creatures you control with total power 4 or more: This Vehicle becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.)', '{2}, {T}: Tap target artifact or creature.', '{2}{U}: Scry 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put that card on the bottom of your library.)', '{3}{G}: Put a +1/+1 counter on Verdant Automaton.', '{3}{R}: Welder Automaton deals 1 damage to each opponent.', '{3}{U}, {T}, Tap X untapped artifacts you control: Look at the top X cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', "{4}{W}: Return another target creature you control to its owner's hand.", '{7}, {T}, Sacrifice Universal Solvent: Destroy target permanent.', "{7}: Create a token that's a copy of target artifact. That token gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step.", '{8}, {T}: Search your library for a permanent card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', '{B}, Sacrifice Implement of Malice: Target player discards a card. Activate only as a sorcery.\\nWhen Implement of Malice is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, draw a card.', '{G}, Sacrifice Implement of Ferocity: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature. Activate only as a sorcery.\\nWhen Implement of Ferocity is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, draw a card.', '{R}, Sacrifice Implement of Combustion: It deals 1 damage to target player or planeswalker.\\nWhen Implement of Combustion is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, draw a card.', '{T}, Sacrifice an artifact: Embraal Gear-Smasher deals 2 damage to each opponent.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Activate only if you control an artifact.', '{T}: Add {G}.', '{T}: Target opponent loses 1 life. If you control a Tezzeret planeswalker, that player loses 3 life instead.', '{T}: You get {E} (an energy counter).\\n{T}, Pay {E}{E}{E}: Consulate Turret deals 2 damage to target player or planeswalker.', '{U}, Sacrifice Implement of Examination: Draw a card.\\nWhen Implement of Examination is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, draw a card.', '{W}, Sacrifice Implement of Improvement: You gain 2 life.\\nWhen Implement of Improvement is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, draw a card.', '{W}, Sacrifice Restoration Specialist: Return up to one target artifact card and up to one target enchantment card from your graveyard to your hand.']
flavor: ['"A few drops of this, and the trickiest problems simply melt away."\\n—Thamaz, Weldfast inventor', '"A key weakness in the design is its vulnerability to repeated, forceful blows."', '"A perfect fusion of nature and artifice."\\n—Irsi, Kujar gardener', '"A well-made wrench is a versatile, indispensable tool."', '"Aether is the soul of Kaladesh, and all souls should be free."', '"After I examine your cargo and check your papers, you can be on your way."', '"All buildings are subject to search. Resistance will be punished."\\n—Enforcer-Chief Ranaj', '"As a kid, I dreamed of flying on those wild drakes. They inspired me to build wings of my own."\\n—Nadja Cloudtoucher, aerowright', '"As this conflict grows, it gets harder to prevent the city from breaking down. How much longer can we keep this machinery balanced?"', '"Before we can destroy our enemies, we must find them. We must peer into every wretched hovel and every teeming market."\\n—Baral, Chief of Compliance', '"Being an inventor means knowing how to use the tools at hand to make something great—or to bring it down."\\n—Pia Nalaar', '"Catch me if you can."', '"Control the Great Conduit? You might as well try to divert a river with your hands."', '"Death might come tomorrow, but today—today I am alive."', '"Each creature holds a solution to a problem, a lesson to be learned."\\n—Oviya Pashiri, sage lifecrafter', '"Get out of my way."', '"Give me eight walkers, I\'ll give you the city."\\n—Dovin Baan', '"Go forth and cause trouble, my little one!"', '"Hit where it hurts, and always hit first."', '"How easily your flames are quenched."\\n—Baral, Chief of Compliance', '"I am confident that all our enterprises can benefit from this little revolution."', '"I can no longer sit in my workshop and ignore the events outside. My hammers strike for the people of Ghirapur."', '"I didn\'t survive that crash just so I could fall to the likes of you."', '"I do not ask you to be tame. I only ask you to be true."\\n—Rishkar, Peema renegade', '"I do not need to pierce your heart to still its beating."', '"I don\'t think they\'ll appreciate my . . . adjustments."\\n—Karavin, renegade saboteur', '"I was made for this!"', '"I will go where the lion-man leads."', '"I will not rest until every vestige of the Consulate—every banner, flag, and standard—has fallen."', '"I\'ve made some fine acquisitions of late, so I\'m planning to make commensurate improvements to my security systems. I have a consultant coming tomorrow."\\n—Kurna Majan, Luminary League', '"If nothing else, the Inventors\' Fair taught us that we\'re only beginning to discover aether\'s true potential."\\n—Kershan Danil, Highspire artisan', '"If the Consulate has abandoned restraint, so too shall the wilds."\\n—Surash, keeper of the Cowl', '"If you can build it, we can move it."\\n—Bes Tavani, Bomat merchant', '"Inspiration is found by looking outward."\\n—Oviya Pashiri, sage lifecrafter', '"It came to rest upon the angel\'s arm, and then the weight of their gazes fell upon me."\\n—Aeronaut\'s journal', '"It is fascinating to see how the people of this plane replicate magical techniques without a natural gift. Also frustrating."\\n—Jace Beleren', '"It is finished. Now the real work can begin."\\n—Tezzeret', '"It is folly to believe your precious inventions will endure. All things return to the soil."\\n—Nirav, Tirahar elder', '"It seems there\'s even better hunting down here."', '"It was made, yes, but that does not mean it cannot grow."', '"It was right here a second ago . . ."', '"It\'s important to always have the right tool for the job. This one is for picking my teeth."', '"It\'s like they planted another Bastion right in the middle of the harbor."\\n—Bes Tavani, Bomat merchant', '"It\'s natural, it\'s all around us, and it\'s there for the taking. Just try and tell me what I\'m doing is wrong."', '"Let\'s add just a bit more stopping power."', '"Let\'s err on the side of glorious mayhem."', '"Let\'s just broaden its surveillance lens."', '"One head watches for Consulate enforcers. The other watches for renegade thieves."\\n—Crime Lord Gonti', '"One look at this glorious item convinced me that Kaladesh deserved my full attention. Sure enough, my time here has yielded exquisite fruit."\\n—Tezzeret', '"Our watchtowers are well positioned. Why don\'t we arm them?"\\n—Enforcer-Chief Ranaj', '"Peace? Its sole purpose is fear."\\n—Saheeli Rai', '"Regards from Peema."\\n—Rishkar', '"Slow the Consulate with whatever you\'ve got!"\\n—Jasi Ganin, master siphoner', '"Success is found where others fear to look."\\n—Ara, renegade smuggler', '"Supplies inbound. Keep that pressure on."', '"Sure, you know the law. But I know the streets."', '"The Consulate pushed me to my limit, darling, and this is the result."', '"The Consulate sought to crush us. Let\'s give them a taste of their own medicine."\\n—Venkat Dasai, renegade commander', '"The Great Conduit connects us all."', '"The echo of silence is music to my ears."', '"The most harmonious designs are based on relationships found in nature."\\n—Venand Kapur, the Gearherder', '"The time for subtlety is over, darling."', '"The tools of the past will help us forge the future."', '"The wild tangle of the Cowl provides sanctuary to life that watched the first buildings rise."', '"The workshops are silent. Our creations have been seized. They have killed what made us alive."\\n—Pia Nalaar', '"There is no greater coward than one who believes in nothing."', '"They never tire, they never complain, and they never ask questions. Build more."\\n—Ivash, Consulate inventor', '"This armor transcends the limitations of mere flesh and bone."', '"This fight belongs to us all."', '"This is about more than aether or inventions. Tezzeret\'s schemes must be stopped!"\\n—Ajani Goldmane', '"This is bigger than you. All of you."\\n—Tezzeret', '"This little critter can turn all of you to scrap in under thirty seconds! Come on, who wants to be the first to go? Try and stop me!"', '"To survive up here, I\'ve learned when to use my harpoon and when to just enjoy the view."\\n—Kadhu, skywhaler', '"Too little, too late. The machine is in motion."\\n—Tezzeret', '"Until all have found their place, I will keep watch."', '"We have safe houses in every zone, but you\'ll never find one without this."', '"We\'ve been through a lot together."', '"When everything hangs on a single moment, be sure you choose the right moment."\\n—Jace Beleren', '"Wherever the strong would harm the weak, I will be there."\\n—Ajani Goldmane', '"Will you be strong and stand with me?"', '"With spy thopters all around, how can the consuls be so blind to Tezzeret\'s manipulations?"\\n—Gideon Jura', '"You can tell me what I want to know, or you can talk to the Chief of Compliance. Why don\'t you make it easy on yourself?"', '"You can\'t hope to comprehend the plans that are in motion."\\n—Tezzeret', '"You never know what day might be your last."', '"You want to know what we are fighting for? Look at the wonder in that child\'s eyes."\\n—Pia Nalaar', 'A beacon of prosperity to some, a shadow of oppression to others.', 'A dream of fire lies coiled inside, waiting for its glorious awakening.', 'A few aetherborn have discovered a way to sustain their own existences at the cost of an insatiable hunger for the life essence of other beings.', 'A hermit crab goes through many shells in its lifetime, and not all are natural in origin.', 'A living invention born of a grand design.', 'A mystery in metal.', 'A tool to see the unseen.', "Aboard her ship, the *Dragon's Smile*, Kari follows no one's rules but her own.", 'Aether currents in the sky mirror water currents below, including the deadly rapids.', 'As renegade forces closed in on the Aether Spire, Consulate blockades failed one by one.', "As the rebellion spread, renegade ingenuity outpaced the Consulate's greatest fears.", 'Beyond the chaos of Ghirapur lies a vibrant world where aether flows through nature.', "Bitter the bite of a demon's steel, and deep the abyss it opens.", 'Chandra was driven by her anger, directed particularly at the man who had taken her father from her.', 'Comrades in life. Comrades in death.', 'Conflict breeds opportunity.', "Despite the magic that sustains Gonti's life, the crime lord is often described as heartless.", 'Duplication is neither thievery nor flattery. It is efficiency.', "Dwarves' tools are priceless heirlooms handed down through generations.", 'Elvish weavers use spidersilk to make everything from tapestries to rappelling ropes.', 'Escapes should always be daring.', "For some of Ghirapur's aerowrights, building thopters is a byproduct of larger construction efforts.", "Ghirapur's most celebrated inventors have been immortalized in clockwork.", 'Gremlins are loyal to nothing but their next meal.', 'Gremlins can change from pest to problem to plague in the span of a moment.', 'Gremlins in the wild feed on nodules of pure aether, which are also prized by miners.', "Headquartered at the Bastion of the Honorable, the Consulate's enforcers are charged with the impossible task of keeping the peace.", 'Illegal street races turned out to be perfect practice for avoiding Consulate patrols.', 'In the cellars beneath Narnam House, a strange and deadly garden grows.', "In the hold of the *Heart of Kiran*, Chandra answered Dovin Baan's sabotage with an explosive retort.", 'It is the nature of the strong to survive.', "Its buzzing is easily mistaken for the hum of a thopter's wings.", "Its elaborate designs reveal secrets of aether's flow.", 'Its frill inspired the design of efficient aether collectors.', 'Living so close to death gives the aetherborn an unusual perspective on risk.', 'Many airship captains keep pets that share their love of the sky.', 'Many veterans of the Ovalchase racetrack turned their talents to the renegade cause.', "Most of the constructs the renegades used against the Consulate weren't originally intended for combat. But some didn't require much modification.", 'Perfect for getting through to the consuls.', "Pia's passion was directed at the big picture—at making real, lasting change.", 'Renegade supply lines are, by necessity, mobile and difficult to disrupt.', 'Renegades run the gamut from lofty sages to petty thieves.', 'Rules and rails are made to be broken.', 'Shipwrecks do wonders for the local fauna, providing both shelter and aether.', 'Small aeronaut societies like the Wind-Kin had little to lose by siding with the renegades, and much to gain.', 'Some aetherborn joined the rebellion for profit, others for the sake of their freedom, still others for revenge.', 'Subtlety is not a necessary part of sabotage.', "Tezzeret's command of living metal has nothing to do with intricate gearcraft or aether supplies.", 'The "leaking spire" stands for liberation from Consulate control.', "The Consulate had access to thousands of innovative devices displayed at the Inventors' Fair. A few small changes transformed some of them from marvels of ingenuity to instruments of oppression.", 'The Consulate prizes innovation when it is dependable and replicable.', 'The Consulate recruits its best pilots from the League of Aeronauts. Many go on to command entire fleets.', "The Consulate's eyes—unblinking, unsleeping—are everywhere.", 'The Hold, an illegal research facility in a derelict merchant ship, became a wellspring of renegade intelligence.', "The Scrappers, an underground group with a passion for automaton brawls, had renegade leanings even before the Consulate's crackdown. It didn't take long for them to lend their best brawlers to the conflict.", 'The best engineers recognize when a problem has already been solved.', 'The daredevil racers of the Derby Crows, long at odds with the Consulate, were quick to join the renegades in open revolt.', "The dragons perching in Freejam's towers symbolize the zone's fierce independence.", 'The loyalty of a felidar is hard won but worth the effort.', "The renegades mounted an aether disruptor aboard a lightweight thopter to destroy Tezzeret's Planar Bridge.", 'The residents of Embraal were never known for finesse, just for getting things done.', "The streets of Ghirapur have become dangerous. It's good to have a dependable companion.", 'The tools of invention became the weapons of revolution.', 'The vibrant forest of Peema is awash with aether. Its animals are stronger, faster, and more aggressive than their counterparts elsewhere.', 'There is no shortage of illegal salvage in Ghirapur, nor of those who are willing to profit from it.', 'Travelers to Lathnu, high on the Devra Cliffs, need not fear the political strife of Ghirapur . . . but they have other dangers to worry about.', "When fighting spilled over into Giant's Walk, the aether weapons and swooping airships angered the normally placid creatures.", 'When the salvage team brought in the shattered gearhulk, a wave of excitement swept through the renegade foundry.', 'When you have taught an automaton how to build others of its kind, it is a small step to make it build itself.', 'While hunting aether, a gremlin may ignore other stimuli, including threats to its own life.', "You can't fight what you can't find."]
artist: ['Adam Paquette', 'Anna Steinbauer', 'Anthony Palumbo', 'Bastien L. Deharme', 'Brad Rigney', 'Chase Stone', 'Chris Rahn', 'Chris Rallis', 'Christine Choi', 'Christopher Burdett', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Cliff Childs', 'Clint Cearley', 'Craig J Spearing', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Darek Zabrocki', 'David Palumbo', 'Deruchenko Alexander', 'E. M. Gist', 'Efflam Mercier', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Eytan Zana', 'Filip Burburan', 'Greg Opalinski', 'Howard Lyon', 'Izzy', 'Jaime Jones', 'Jakub Kasper', 'James Paick', 'James Ryman', 'Jason A. Engle', 'Jason Kang', 'Jason Rainville', 'Johann Bodin', 'Johannes Voss', 'John Avon', 'John Severin Brassell', 'John Silva', 'John Stanko', 'Jonas De Ro', 'Joseph Meehan', 'Josh Hass', 'Jung Park', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kieran Yanner', 'Kirsten Zirngibl', 'Lake Hurwitz', 'Lius Lasahido', 'Magali Villeneuve', 'Mathias Kollros', 'Matt Stewart', 'Mike Bierek', 'Min Yum', 'Raoul Vitale', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Ryan Alexander Lee', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Ryan Yee', 'Sam Burley', 'Sara Winters', 'Scott Murphy', 'Shreya Shetty', 'Sidharth Chaturvedi', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Steve Argyle', 'Steven Belledin', 'Sung Choi', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Titus Lunter', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Tomasz Jedruszek', 'Tommy Arnold', 'Tony Foti', 'Tyler Jacobson', 'Victor Adame Minguez', 'Viktor Titov', 'Vincent Proce', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Wesley Burt', 'Winona Nelson', 'Yongjae Choi', 'Zack Stella', 'Zezhou Chen']
